/* book Worked example: Q: At 300 K and 50 bar, a pure gas has fugacity coefficient φ = 0.90. Calculate its residual molar Gibbs energy GR. Use R = 8.314 J/(mol K).
   1. Write the relation: GR = RT ln φ.
   2. Compute RT: 8.314 × 300 = 2494.2 J/mol.
   3. Compute ln φ: ln(0.90) = −0.10536.
   4. Multiply: GR = 2494.2 × (−0.10536) = −262.8 J/mol.
   Answer: GR = −262.8 J/mol; the real gas has lower Gibbs energy than the ideal gas at 300 K and 50 bar. */
